flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1["Complete the following checks: 1. Inspect the<br/>suction cup sealing face for cuts, abrasion, or<br/>permanent set. 2. Check the bellows body for cracks<br/>or delamination. 3. Inspect the cup mounting thread<br/>for cross threading or stripping."]
    box_2[/"Refer to the cup replacement interval schedule."/]
    box_3{"Cup structural integrity acceptable?"}
    box_4(["End, Replace cups: cracking or deformation detected"])
    box_5["With the vacuum system de energised, physically<br/>inspect every push to connect fitting and<br/>compression nut on the suction circuit from the<br/>generator to the cup ports. Tighten any loose<br/>fittings by hand plus a quarter turn. Check all<br/>tubing for kinks, cuts, or heat distortion that<br/>could cause partial flow restriction."]
    box_6["Press the suction cup firmly against a clean flat<br/>reference surface and start the vacuum generator.<br/>Using a calibrated vacuum gauge connected at the cup<br/>port, read the steady state vacuum level after five<br/>seconds. Record the value and compare against the<br/>minimum rated holding vacuum in the gripper<br/>specification. Note the time taken to reach steady<br/>state as an indicator of circuit leakage."]
    box_7{"Vacuum holding level within specification?"}
    box_8["Clean cup seating face and replace cup seal"]
    box_9{"Reverify vacuum level after seal replacement"}
    box_10(["End, Escalate: vacuum generator fault suspected"])
    box_11["Connect a calibrated inline flow meter to the blow<br/>off supply upstream of the solenoid valve. Trigger a<br/>single blow off cycle and record peak flow rate in<br/>litres per minute. Compare the reading against the<br/>rated flow at the supply pressure shown on the<br/>regulator gauge. Repeat three times and average the<br/>results."]
    box_12[/"Refer to the vacuum system flow specification."/]
    box_13{"Vacuum flow rate within rated range?"}
    box_14["Clean or replace flow restrictor fitting"]
    box_15["Using a photoelectric sensor or a stopwatch<br/>triggered from the solenoid valve signal, measure<br/>the elapsed time from blow off command to part clear<br/>of the cup. Record the release time and compare<br/>against the maximum permitted release time in the<br/>cycle specification. Unusually long release times<br/>indicate cup face contamination or low blow off<br/>flow."]
    box_16{"Part release cycle, 10 consecutive picks successful?"}
    box_17["Adjust pick cycle parameters, dwell time and vacuum<br/>delay"]
    box_18["Remove the blow off nozzle from the cup assembly and<br/>inspect the orifice for coolant deposits, swarf, or<br/>corrosion scaling. Soak the nozzle in warm detergent<br/>solution for five minutes, then clear the orifice<br/>with a wire of the correct gauge. Reinstall and test<br/>blow off flow before returning to service."]
    box_19{"Blow off pressure within range?"}
    box_20["Adjust blow off pressure regulator"]
    box_21["Log test results and update maintenance record"]
    box_22(["End, Procedure complete"])
    box_23["Second seal replacement attempt: remove the suction<br/>cup body completely and replace the cup seal, the<br/>body O ring, and all push to connect fitting O rings<br/>in the vacuum circuit with new parts from a sealed<br/>service kit. Reconnect all fittings to the correct<br/>torque value and verify that no fitting is cross<br/>threaded before repeating the vacuum level test."]

